.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Book snapshots were ignored as "high-volume and regenerable". Both halves of that were
# wrong. They are ~1.5 MB/day, and they are the one thing here that cannot be regenerated
# at all: a book at an instant that has passed is gone. Since 2026-10-11 collection runs
# on ephemeral runners with no disk that outlives the job, so this store is tracked --
# which also upgrades the point-in-time claim from "a job wrote this live, trust us" to a
# GitHub commit timestamp, and that is third-party attestation.
data/cache/

# Run logs.
*.log

# Scoring output. Regenerable from the database, and a committed report is a
# claim about a sample size that has since moved.
reports/

# Wrangler's local state and dependencies. The pinger itself is four tracked files and has
# no dependencies of its own -- wrangler is installed globally or run via npx.
pinger/.wrangler/
pinger/node_modules/
